The prose samples in this directory are NOT covered by the repository's MIT
licence. They are text from English Wikipedia, reproduced under:

    Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0)
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

Every sample is pinned to an immutable revision id. ATTRIBUTION.json lists the
source page title, revision id, timestamp, and a permalink that resolves to
exactly the text vendored here.

Share-alike travels with these files. If you redistribute them, or a derivative
of them, that redistribution is CC BY-SA 4.0 — not MIT.

The scanner, the tests, and everything else in this repository remain MIT.
Only the contents of tests/corpus/ai/ and tests/corpus/human/ are affected.

Nothing may be added to this directory except text under a compatible free
licence, with provenance recorded the same way. Not contemporary journalism,
not books, not blogs, not anyone's private writing, however good a sample it
would make.
